Since the F14 name swap (commit cd86036, 2026-06-11): the user-facing entry
is the repo-root `./andes-sim` bash wrapper (self-builds `build/andes-sim`
via scripts/build_driver.sh on first use). The Python reference driver was
renamed `hsim` -> `hsim.py`, frozen as the byte-parity golden. Its argparse
sets `prog="hsim"` explicitly, so the rename changed no output bytes.
`tests/andes_sim/parity.sh` defaults `GOLDEN=$ROOT/hsim.py`.

Still golden-only (no C++ port yet): the SimPoint pipeline -- `run --mode
simpoint`, `estimate`, `profile`, `cluster`, `archive`, `replay` (driver
F11/F13). Docs reference those as `./hsim.py ...` on purpose.

Doctor hint strings ("run ./andes-sim build") must stay in LOCKSTEP between
hsim.py and driver/cmd_doctor.cpp or doctor parity breaks. The env var
HSIM_MMAP_DIR keeps its old name -- it is functional API both drivers read
(driver/shm.cpp:85), not a name reference. Related:
[[project_hsim_cpp_rewrite]].
